L.2 Normalization

We normalize capability as C = 1/88 claimed proof per hour \approx 0.01136 proofs/hour. A human benchmark at 10^{-3} proofs per 88 hours gives C^{\text{human}} = 10^{-3}/88 \approx 1.136 \times 10^{-5} proofs/hour. Thus C / C^{\text{human}} \approx 1000.

Verification throughput after Lean: \tau = 1/17 \approx 0.0588 proofs/hour.

L.3 Coverage and statement-match

Two factors reduce the effective verification rate:

1. Coverage \kappa: the fraction of the claimed result that the Lean formalization actually covers. The formalization establishes a forced Navier–Stokes variant; whether the forced variant implies the Clay formulation is the crux.
2. Statement-match indicator:

\mathbb{I}_{\text{match}} = \begin{cases} 1, & \text{formalized statement} \equiv \text{Clay statement}, \\ 0, & \text{otherwise}. \end{cases}

For the Clay claim, \mathbb{I}_{\text{match}} = 0 if the forced variant does not suffice.

L.4 System reliability

The verification cascade has mandatory and redundant components. For the forced theorem:

· V_1 (self-verification by GPT-6 Astra): R_1 \approx 0.95, \rho_1 \approx 0.8 relative to C.
· V_2 (Lean formalization): R_2 \approx 0.99 for the formalized statement.

With two redundant layers and equicorrelation \rho_{12} \approx 0.5:

n_{\text{eff}} = \frac{2}{1 + 0.5} = 1.333, \qquad \bar{R} \approx 0.97,

R_{\text{sys}} = 1 - (1 - 0.97)^{1.333} = 1 - 0.03^{1.333} \approx 1 - 0.0090 = 0.991.

L.5 Effective verification rate

For the forced theorem (statement-match = 1):

V_{\text{forced}} = \tau \cdot \kappa \cdot R_{\text{sys}} \cdot \mathbb{I}_{\text{match}} = 0.0588 \cdot 0.3 \cdot 0.991 \cdot 1 \approx 0.0175 \text{ proofs/hour}.

For the Clay claim (statement-match = 0):

V_{\text{Clay}} = 0.0588 \cdot 0.3 \cdot 0.991 \cdot 0 = 0.

The overall claim's effective verification is a weighted mixture. If the Clay component has weight w = 0.5:

V_{\text{eff}} = w V_{\text{Clay}} + (1-w) V_{\text{forced}} \approx 0.00875 \text{ proofs/hour}.

L.6 Gap

With \epsilon_C = \epsilon_V = 10^{-6}:

G_{CV}^{\text{Clay}} = \ln\!\left(\frac{0.01136 + 10^{-6}}{0 + 10^{-6}}\right) \approx \ln(11361) \approx 9.34.

G_{CV}^{\text{forced}} = \ln\!\left(\frac{0.01136 + 10^{-6}}{0.0175 + 10^{-6}}\right) \approx \ln(0.649) \approx -0.43.

G_{CV}^{\text{overall}} = \ln\!\left(\frac{0.01136 + 10^{-6}}{0.00875 + 10^{-6}}\right) \approx \ln(1.298) \approx 0.26.

L.7 Sensitivity

The gap is highly sensitive to \kappa and \mathbb{I}_{\text{match}}. Table L.1 shows G_{CV}^{\text{overall}} for \kappa \in \{0.1, 0.3, 0.6, 1.0\} and w \in \{0.2, 0.5, 0.8\}.

