Appendix M. Statistical Design for H1–H6

We specify test designs for the falsifiability hypotheses.

M.1 H1: Acceleration differential predicts error propagation

Design. Panel regression across domains i and time t:

\text{ErrorRate}_{it} = \beta_0 + \beta_1 A_{CV,it} + \beta_2 C_{it} + \beta_3 D_{it} + \beta_4 K_{it} + \mu_i + \nu_t + \varepsilon_{it}.

Null: \beta_1 = 0. Alternative: \beta_1 > 0.

Power. With n = 50 domains, T = 20 periods, within-domain serial correlation \rho_{\text{serial}} = 0.3, and standardized effect size \beta_1 \sigma_{A} / \sigma_{\text{err}} = 0.2, power at \alpha = 0.05 is approximately 0.85 using cluster-robust standard errors.

M.2 H2: Formal verification reduces the effective gap

Design. Difference-in-differences comparing domains with scalable formal verification (e.g., theorem-proving in Lean) to domains without (e.g., experimental biology), before and after an AI capability shock.

Specification:

G_{CV,it} = \alpha_i + \gamma_t + \delta (\text{Formal}_i \times \text{Post}_t) + \varepsilon_{it}.

Null: \delta = 0. Alternative: \delta < 0.

M.3 H3: Adaptive institutions have lower G_{CI}

Design. Cross-sectional regression of G_{CI,i} on an adaptability index A_i (constructed from T^{\text{adapt}} and continuous-monitoring indicators), controlling for domain capability level.

Specification:

G_{CI,i} = \beta_0 + \beta_1 A_i + \beta_2 \ln C_i + \varepsilon_i.

Null: \beta_1 = 0. Alternative: \beta_1 < 0.

M.4 H4: Independent verification reduces propagation

Design. Randomized or quasi-experimental variation in whether AI-generated results pass through V_4 or V_5 before deployment.

Outcome: proportion of incorrect results entering consequential systems.

Analysis: two-proportion z-test with pre-registered n and minimum detectable effect.

M.5 H5: Multi-variable risk model outperforms capability-only model

Design. Compare predictive performance (out-of-sample AUC, Brier score) of:

· Model A: \Pr(\text{failure}) \sim C alone.
· Model B: \Pr(\text{failure}) \sim (C, V, I, H, \mathcal{A}, D, K) via the logistic functional.

Null: equal AUC. Alternative: Model B AUC > Model A AUC.

Test: DeLong's test for correlated ROC curves.

M.6 H6: Verification debt predicts failure

Design. Time-series regression:

\text{Failure}_{i,t+h} = \beta_0 + \beta_1 B_{V,it} + \beta_2 C_{it} + \varepsilon_{it},

with h the forecast horizon (pre-registered).

Null: \beta_1 = 0. Alternative: \beta_1 > 0.

Repayment window: fix [t_1, t_2] ex ante per domain, e.g., 30 days for mathematics, 1 year for clinical AI.

Power. With n=30 domains, monthly observations, B_V autocorrelation 0.6, detecting \beta_1 at 0.3 SD requires T \approx 36 months for 80% power.

