Appendix O. Dimensional Consistency Analysis

Proposition O.1 (Capability–verification dimensions). C and V both have dimensions of [outputs]/[time]. The ratio C/V is dimensionless, so G_{CV} and A_{CV} are dimensionless.

Proposition O.2 (Institutional adaptation dimensions). With \sigma dimensionless and T^{\text{adapt}} in [time], I = \sigma \ln 2 / T^{\text{adapt}} has dimensions [time]^{-1}, matching the rate interpretation. The factor \ln 2 is required so that I is the rate constant of an exponential decay with half-life T^{\text{adapt}}.

Proof. If a quantity decays with half-life T_{1/2}, its rate constant is \lambda = \ln 2 / T_{1/2}. ∎

Proposition O.3 (Verification debt dimensions). B_V has dimensions of [outputs] (accumulated proof-equivalents), since it integrates a rate over time.

Proposition O.4 (Risk functional dimensions). All arguments of the logarithms in z_i are dimensionless (after applying floors), so z_i is dimensionless and \sigma_{\text{log}}(z_i) is well-defined.

Proposition O.5 (Correlation parameter dimensions). \rho is a correlation coefficient, hence dimensionless.

Proposition O.6 (Depreciation rate dimensions). \lambda has dimensions [time]^{-1}, consistent with its role in e^{-\lambda(t-s)}.

